⍝ D-97: ⍬ is the empty numeric vector
🍎> ⍴⍬
⍝ expect: 0
🍎> ≡⍬
⍝ expect: 1
🍎> ⍬≡0⍴0
⍝ expect: 1
🍎> ⍴1 ⍬ 2
⍝ expect: 3
🍎> ⍴⍬ ⍬
⍝ expect: 2
⍝ D-98: the set functions compare elements by match and keep the left argument's order
🍎> 1 2 3 4 5∼2 3 4
⍝ expect: 1 5
🍎> 'RHYME'∼'MYTH'
⍝ expect: RE
🍎> 'GO' 'TO' 'IT'∼'GOTO' 'IT'
⍝ expect: 'GO' 'TO'
🍎> ⍴4 5 ⍬ 6 7∼9 5 3 7
⍝ expect: 3
🍎> 1 2 3 4∩3 4 5 6
⍝ expect: 3 4
🍎> 4 3 2 1∩3 4 5 6
⍝ expect: 4 3
🍎> 'we' 'are' 'so'∩'are' 'so' 'x'
⍝ expect: 'are' 'so'
🍎> ∪1 1 2 2 3 3 4 4 1 2 3 4
⍝ expect: 1 2 3 4
🍎> ∪'mississippi'
⍝ expect: misp
⍝ A∪B is ∪A,B (GNU APL), so duplicates leave both sides
🍎> 1 1 2 2∪1 1 3 3 5 5
⍝ expect: 1 2 3 5
🍎> 4 3 2 1∪3 4 5 6
⍝ expect: 4 3 2 1 5 6
⍝ an empty result keeps the left argument's prototype (D-77)
🍎> ⍴''∪⍬
⍝ expect: 0
🍎> ⍴↑(0⍴⊂'ab')∪⍬
⍝ expect: 2
🍎> ⍴↑(0⍴⊂'ab')∩⍬
⍝ expect: 2
🍎> (2 2⍴1)∼1
⍝ refuse: %rank-error
🍎> ∪2 2⍴1
⍝ refuse: %rank-error
⍝ the ASCII words (D-8)
🍎> )ASCII ON
⍝ expect: ascii ON
🍎> rho zilde
⍝ expect: 0
🍎> 1 2 downshoe 2 3
⍝ expect: 1 2 3
🍎> 1 2 3 upshoe 2
⍝ expect: 2
🍎> )ASCII OFF
⍝ expect: ascii OFF
